{%- comment -%}
  GDRock consent blocker + cookie banner for Shopify.

  Install (Online Store > Themes > current theme > Edit code):
    1. Add this file as snippets/gdrock-blocker.liquid.
    2. In layout/theme.liquid, make this the FIRST line after <head>,
       above {{ content_for_header }} and above every other script:
         {% render 'gdrock-blocker' %}
    3. Delete any older GDRock <script> tag from the theme.
    4. Settings > Customer privacy: require consent for the regions you sell to.

  Why first: Shopify writes app embeds, the pixel manager and window.Shopify
  inside {{ content_for_header }}. Anything that runs before GDRock is not
  blocked, and GDRock has to catch window.Shopify the moment it is created
  to pass the visitor's choice to Shopify's Customer Privacy API.

  No async or defer on the tag: it must run before the rest of <head>.
  The site id is the shop's primary domain without "www."; if your GDRock
  site id is different, type it in place of the Liquid below.

  After installing, open the shop, press F12 and run GDRock.installFix()
  in the console for anything left to change (for example an app embed,
  such as Klaviyo's, that must be switched off and pasted in tagged).
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="https://cdn.gdrock.com/gdrock.js" data-site-id="{{ shop.domain | remove_first: 'www.' }}"></script>
